//! The michael.slop skull, traced out of the mascot sprite.
//!
//! GENERATED by `gen_skull.py` from
//! `site/static/icons/skeleton.png`, region (9, 0) 23x19.
//!
//! The X region is app.js's, less one column of dark padding at the front
//! and two at the back -- a tighter silhouette, with no bone lost (measured:
//! the old trace had 3 bone-free columns left and 2 right). The
//! HEIGHT is two rows shorter on purpose: app.js takes 21 rows, of which
//! the last two are the neck stub below the teeth. Head alone is the
//! cleaner silhouette, and it stops the jump lifting a floating neck.
//!
//! Cells are LABELS, not pixels:
//!
//!   ` ` air   `#` bone   `.` dark (outline, eye sockets, nose, tooth gaps)
//!
//! The dark cells must stay dark at every angle and every light level, or
//! the sockets fill in and the face stops reading as a face. That is a
//! property of the drawing, which is why the labels are stored rather than
//! a finished picture.

